course: dictionary
lesson: 2312
title: Crooked: bent or dishonest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Crooked means not straight. It can be bent, twisted or uneven, like crooked teeth, a crooked picture on the wall, or a crooked line. In maths, a crooked line is not a straight line, so you would use a ruler to check.
explain: A crooked person is someone who is dishonest and cheats people. The words around it tell you which meaning fits. A crooked nose is a bent nose, but a crooked man who cheats his customers is a dishonest man.
explain: Tennyson's poem says, «He clasps the crag with crooked hands». An eagle has talons, not hands, so the poet gives it hands. That is personification. The hard c sound in crooked, clasps and crag is alliteration, and it makes the line sound strong.
fact: Crooked means not straight; bent, twisted or uneven.
fact: A crooked person is dishonest and cheats people.
fact: Crooked is an adjective: crooked, more crooked, most crooked. Say it KROOK-id.
fact: «A crooked nose is checked after a few days, when the swelling has gone down.»
fact: In a nursery rhyme, «There was a crooked man» paints a bent, strange shape.
exercise: «Her smile was crooked, higher on one side than the other.» What does crooked mean here? | *Not straight or even | Happy and bright | Dishonest | Very loud
exercise: Tennyson writes «He clasps the crag with crooked hands». Which sound is repeated? | The s sound at the end of a word | The long oo sound | The soft g sound | *The hard c sound
exercise: Sam says the shopkeeper is crooked because he cheats customers. What does crooked mean? | *Dishonest, cheating people | Very tall | Funny and kind | Bent over with age
test: «A crooked nose is checked after a few days, when the swelling has gone down.» What does crooked describe? | A nose that smells of flowers | *A nose that is bent or out of shape | A straight line on a page | Teeth that are bright white
test: In maths, how can you check whether a line is crooked? | Guess by eye | Look at it from far away | *Use a ruler | Ask a friend
exam: Why does Tennyson give the eagle «crooked hands»? | It is a mistake, since eagles have hands | It is a sign the eagle is dishonest | It shows the eagle is very old | *It is personification, since an eagle has talons, not hands
